            <ArticleTitle>[Volvulus of the mobile spleen. Conservative laparoscopic treatment].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1005-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Volvulus of the mobile spleen is a rare condition generally manifested by acute sudden onset abdominal pain localized in the left flank. Ultrasound or computed tomographic imaging generally provides the diagnosis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE REPORT" NlmCategory="METHODS">An 18-year-old patient was hospitalized for acute pain of the left flank that had begun 48 hours earlier. The abdominal scan visualized a volvulus of a mobile spleen. Laparoscopic distortion was successful, allowing normal recoloration of the spleen.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DISCUSSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Rapid intervention is crucial for conservative treatment. Laparoscopic treatment allows distortion manoeuvres and splenopexia using a mesh. This is the first reported case of successful conservative laparoscopic treatment of volvulus of a mobile spleen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
